description:
crates/tampines/src/critical_flow/mod.rs:1-8 reads:

    //! Thin re-export of [`tampines_steam_tables`]'s validated choked-flow
    //! solvers (Homogeneous Equilibrium Model critical flow, validated against
    //! Moody, Zaloudek, and Marviken reference data -- see that crate's own
    //! `CLAUDE.md` and README for the V&V methodology and results).

The Marviken part of that claim is FALSE. In crates/tampines-steam-tables/src/steam_turbine_equations/converging_diverging_nozzles/tests/marviken_tests.rs:

- :116-117  #[test] #[ignore="skip first, Marviken is more complex"] fn validate_against_marviken_test_24()
- the body loops 40 digitised (p, G) points, computes a relative difference and PRINTS it
- :213 the sole assertion is commented out: //assert!(relative_difference.get::<ratio>() < 0.20);
- :215 the function ends in todo!()

So even if un-ignored it would panic and assert nothing. Marviken validation does not exist.

What IS genuinely validated: Moody (1975) Fig. 1 (13 active isobar tests, log10 mass-flux bound) and Zaloudek (~20+ active tests across four files). Note the Moody validator validate_moody_isobar_inner (:315) SKIPS every point that is neither Region 4 nor deeply subcooled, and isobar_pref_0_25 runs in-dome-only.

Fix: reword the doc comment to "Moody and Zaloudek; Marviken data digitised but not yet gated", and do the same wherever tampines-steam-tables' own CLAUDE.md/README repeats the claim. Per the workspace V&V rule, a validation claim must carry methodology AND measured results.

Verified 2026-08-07 against the working tree.
